==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*3 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*5 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 0.67~1 seconds<sup>20f~30f</sup>.
*5 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 0.67~1 seconds<sup>20f~30f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Trolly Blogger]] spawns as the boss.
**20 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**2 [[Capy|Capies]] spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Without proper planning, this stage could get annoying pretty quickly. Nothing a good amount of spam shouldn't be able to handle, though. Try to bring some units with a pretty quick cooldown to serve as meatshields for Capy, or use a first form Ancient Egg for one of your more useless Egg evolutions to serve as your meatshield for Capy.

